                <pb facs="0115" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/705a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-25T13:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. In view of the uncertainties of the moment and our great concern for the
                    safety of American citizens and ships in the Mediterranean the Department
                    requests that you approach Ciano informally and <pb facs="0116" n="107"
                        xml:id="pg107"/> confidentially and state that we would appreciate being
                    kept closely informed of any developments which would affect these American
                    citizens and ships.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
